=== commit message parent
KS-790: the OAuth token grants resolve the user through the pre-auth carve-out, not the RLS-scoped lookup

POST /api/oauth/token holds a code or a refresh token, not a bearer, so no
tenant GUC is seeded when it runs. Both grants looked the user up with
userRepo.getUserById -- the plain, RLS-scoped lookup -- which under migration
039's fail-closed RLS answers nothing pre-auth; the handler reported the empty
result as `invalid_grant: User not found` for EVERY authorization_code grant,
MFA or not, and the refresh grant carried the same call one branch over. The
lookup now goes through getUserByIdPreAuth (the SECURITY DEFINER carve-out the
other pre-auth token flows already use) at both sites. The null guards and the
refresh grant's ACTIVE pin are unchanged.

The broken lookup had masked an authorize-side MFA bypass; that bypass's doors
are all merged, so the mask is no longer load-bearing.

Enabling change, named: verifyRefreshToken comes from the file's existing static
import now instead of an in-handler `require('../services/jwt')`. Under vitest
that runtime require answers "Cannot find module" (Node's require does not
resolve the .ts source), the throw landed in the route's outer catch, and every
refresh-grant case read 500 whatever it asserted -- which is why no test had
ever reached that branch. The built service is unchanged (same function).

Tests (services/auth, vitest run, node v24.7.0, darwin):
- NEW ks790-token-pre-auth-user-lookup.test.ts, raw socket (the ks820-821
  harness shape), 6 cells: both grants mint when only the carve-out can see the
  user and the plain lookup is not consulted; controls -- carve-out also null ->
  both grants still refused; INACTIVE user -> refresh still refused; wrong
  client secret -> 401 before any lookup.
- Red-first at develop 8861e6216: Tests 4 failed | 2 passed (6) -- the
  authorization_code row 400 "User not found" (the ticket's symptom), the three
  refresh rows 500 (the require). Green 6/6 after.
- Whole auth suite 51 files / 691 tests (was 50 / 685). tsc -p services/auth
  rc 0; the new test file type-checked separately rc 0.
- Tampers (unique anchors, restored by content, sha asserted): T1 the
  authorization_code site reverted -> 1 red ("User not found"); T2 the refresh
  site reverted -> 1 red ("User inactive or not found"); T3 a runtime require
  put back -> all 3 refresh rows red.
- ks820-821-token-client-auth-and-apptype.test.ts: one mock entry added
  (getUserByIdPreAuth, the same user its getUserById stub returns) -- its three
  happy rows read 500 against the fixed product because the mock named only the
  old lookup; no assertion changed.

Not covered: a live POST /api/oauth/token under migration 039 on any
environment (the ticket's NOT MEASURED line stands); the four platform suites.

